# Living docs

A change is not done until these three files match the code. Update them in the same work as the implementation — not later.

| Document | Path | Update when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Vision and requirements | `docs/VISION_AND_REQUIREMENTS.md` | Goals, users, scope, or acceptance change |
| Architecture and design | `docs/ARCHITECTURE_AND_DESIGN.md` | Routes, checks, the written plan, hosting, or visual system change |
| Releases | `CHANGELOG.md` | Something ships that a visitor can see |

The in-app pictures live in `src/components/architecture/Diagrams.tsx`. When a view changes, update that SVG and the matching Mermaid block in the architecture document together.

`/vision` and `/architecture` render the `## Summary` section of each document. If the summary is wrong, the page is wrong. `/releases` renders the changelog.

## Every change

1. Read the three docs before editing.
2. Implement the code.
3. Patch the docs: revise the affected requirement or decision, refresh the Summary if a visitor would notice, and add a dated changelog line (`YYYY-MM-DD`).
4. Do not invent a fourth product doc.

```text
BAD: ship a lesson or a route and leave the documents stale
GOOD: the same change updates the requirement and the release note
```
